sxml validate - Validate XML documents against an XSD 1.1 schema or Schematron rules

Usage: sxml validate [--schema=SCHEMA]... [--schematron=SCH] [--phase=PHASE] [--schematron-param=NAME=VALUE]... [--use-schema-location] [--mode=MODE] [--format=FORMAT] FILE...

Validates each FILE against the XSD 1.1 schema that the SCHEMA
documents form, together with every document they include, import,
redefine or override (local files, relative to the document that
refers to them). Each FILE is parsed and validated in one pass; no
document is written.

With --use-schema-location, the schema documents that a FILE's
xsi:schemaLocation and xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation attributes
name (local files, relative to the FILE) join the SCHEMA documents
in the schema of that FILE, for the namespaces those do not have;
--schema may then be left out. Without it, such hints are not
followed. Errors in a hinted document are reported for the FILE.

The schema is compiled first. Each of its errors is reported on
standard error as
  SCHEMA:LINE:COLUMN: CONSTRAINT: description
and then no FILE is read. Prints nothing when every FILE is valid.
Each error in a FILE is reported as
  FILE:LINE:COLUMN: CONSTRAINT: description
every error, not only the first. CONSTRAINT is the name XSD 1.1
gives the rule, such as cvc-complex-type.2.4. A FILE that is not
well-formed is reported as 'sxml check' reports it.

With --mode=strict (the default) the document element of each FILE
must have a global declaration in the schema. With --mode=lax a
document element without one is assessed laxly: what has a
declaration is validated, and the validity of the FILE is "not
known": it is reported, but does not fail. With --format=json, one
JSON object on standard output lists the schema and every FILE
with its "status" and "errors".

With --schematron, the Schematron schema SCH (ISO/IEC 19757-3:2025;
query bindings xslt, xslt2, xslt3, xslt4, xpath, xpath2, xpath3,
xpath31 and xpath4) is compiled after the XSD schema, with the phase
--phase names and the values --schematron-param gives its schema
parameters; each of its errors is reported as
  SCH:LINE:COLUMN: CODE: description
and then no FILE is read. --schema may then be left out. The rules
run over each FILE (over its validated copy when it is valid against
the XSD schema); each finding is reported as
  FILE:LINE:COLUMN: ID LEVEL: MESSAGE (SCH:LINE:COLUMN)
where ID is the assertion's id (else assert or report) and LEVEL its
severity, else its flag, else its role. A finding whose severity,
else role or flag, is fatal or error, or that has none of them,
makes the FILE invalid. With --format=json each FILE also lists its
"findings" and the "phase" in force; --format=svrl writes the SVRL
report of the one FILE on standard output.

Exit status: 0 when every FILE is valid (or not known, with
--mode=lax); 1 when the schema, the Schematron schema or a FILE is
invalid or a FILE is not well-formed; 3 when a SCHEMA, the SCH or a
FILE cannot be read; 4 when a limit is exceeded or validation needs a
feature sxml does not have yet.

Options:
  -h, --help                         Show this help and exit
      --schema=SCHEMA                XSD schema document; - reads standard input (repeatable)
      --schematron=SCH               Schematron schema; - reads standard input
      --phase=PHASE                  Schematron phase: an id, #ALL, #ANY or #DEFAULT (the default)
      --schematron-param=NAME=VALUE  Value of a Schematron schema parameter, a query fragment (repeatable)
      --use-schema-location          Also read the schema documents a FILE's xsi:schemaLocation names
      --mode=MODE                    Assessment of the document element (one of: strict, lax; default: strict)
      --format=FORMAT                Report format (one of: text, json, svrl; default: text)

Arguments:
  FILE  XML document to validate; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml validate --schema=draft.xsd draft.xml
  sxml validate --schema=draft.xsd invalid.xml
  sxml validate --schema=draft.xsd --format=json draft.xml
  sxml validate --use-schema-location hinted-draft.xml
  sxml validate --schematron=rules.sch draft.xml
  sxml validate --schema=draft.xsd --schematron=rules.sch --phase=#ANY --format=json draft.xml
  sxml validate --schematron=rules.sch --format=svrl draft.xml
